Phase 20f — break test of the pairing rule in scripts/fold-cost.py.
Each clause is neutered in turn by replacing its `problems.append(` with a
same-length no-op, the gate is run, and the file is restored from git.

READ THE COMMIT 879daff BEFORE TRUSTING AN EARLIER VERSION OF THIS LOG. The
first two runs of this harness were measuring a stale bytecode cache: all five
broken variants are byte-identical in size and the loop finishes inside one
second, so CPython served the previous compile. The gates now write no cache;
this harness also removes scripts/__pycache__ before every run, belt and braces.

